		return gx.Frag(Example(ExampleProps{Item: "label", Name: "label-plain", Label: "Label: Plain", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n```gx\n<label.Label for=\"email\">Email</label.Label>\n```\n\n")}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## Installation\n\n"), docs.Tabs(docs.TabsProps{Sync: "install", Children: gx.Frag(docs.TabItem(docs.TabItemProps{Label: "CLI", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\nRun the command in the app module.\n\n```sh frame=\"terminal\" title=\"Terminal\"\ngx add label\n```\n\nThe command writes these files.\n\n| File | Path in the app |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Label.gx` | `ui/label/Label.gx` |\n| `Label.fixtures.go` | `ui/label/Label.fixtures.go` |\n| `styles.go` | `ui/label/styles.go` |\n\n")}), docs.TabItem(docs.TabItemProps{Label: "Manual", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\nCopy each file to its path in the app. Change each import of a registry package to the path of that package in the app.\n\n```gx title=\"ui/label/Label.gx\"\npackage label\n\nprops {\n  // For is the id of the control that the label names. Empty omits the for attribute.\n  For      string = \"\"\n  // Class adds classes to the root element.\n  Class    string = \"\"\n  // Children is the label text.\n  Children gx.Node\n  // Attrs adds HTML attributes to the root element.\n  Attrs    gx.Attrs = nil\n}\n\n<label data-slot=\"label\" class={gx.Cx(\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm leading-none font-medium select-none group-data-[disabled=true]:pointer-events-none group-data-[disabled=true]:opacity-50 peer-disabled:cursor-not-allowed peer-disabled:opacity-50\", p.Class)} {...p.attrs()}>{p.Children}</label>\n```\n\n```go title=\"ui/label/Label.fixtures.go\"\npackage label\n\nimport \"github.com/alternayte/gx\"\n\nvar LabelFixtures = gx.Fixtures[LabelProps]{\n\t\"Plain\": {For: \"email\", Children: gx.Text(\"Email\")},\n}\n```\n\n```go title=\"ui/label/styles.go\"\npackage label\n\nimport \"github.com/alternayte/gx\"\n\n// attrs returns the for attribute when the label names a control, then the\n// caller's attributes.\nfunc (p LabelProps) attrs() gx.Attrs {\n\tif p.For == \"\" {\n\t\treturn p.Attrs\n\t}\n\treturn append(gx.Attrs{{Key: \"for\", Value: p.For}}, p.Attrs...)\n}\n```\n\n")}))}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## Usage\n\n```gx\n<label.Label for=\"email\">Email</label.Label>\n<input id=\"email\" name=\"email\" type=\"email\" />\n```\n\nThe label dims when its control is a disabled `peer`, or when a parent `group` has `data-disabled=\"true\"`.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Plain\n\n"), Example(ExampleProps{Item: "label", Name: "label-plain", Label: "Label: Plain", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n```gx\n<label.Label for=\"email\">Email</label.Label>\n```\n\n")}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## API reference\n\nA tag sets a prop by its name with a lower-case first letter: `Class` is `class`.\n\n### label.Label\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `For` | `string` | `\"\"` | For is the id of the control that the label names. Empty omits the for attribute. |\n| `Class` | `string` | `\"\"` | Class adds classes to the root element. |\n| `Children` | `gx.Node` | Required | Children is the label text. |\n| `Attrs` | `gx.Attrs` | `nil` | Attrs adds HTML attributes to the root element. |\n\n## Do and do not\n\n"), docs.CardGrid(docs.CardGridProps{Children: gx.Frag(docs.Card(docs.CardProps{Title: "Do", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n- Point `For` at the id of the control.\n- Keep the label short.\n\n")}), docs.Card(docs.CardProps{Title: "Don't", Children: gxContentMarkdown("\n\n- Do not use placeholder text as the only label.\n- Do not point `For` at an element that is not a form control.\n\n")}))}), gxContentMarkdown("\n\n## Keyboard\n\n| Key | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| (none) | Clicking the label moves focus to its control. |\n"))
